<title>JORDAN: Aqaba port discharges 7,250 T durum wheat for Iraq.</title>
<headline>Aqaba port discharges 7,250 T durum wheat for Iraq.</headline>
<dateline>AMMAN 1996-12-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>A vessel with 7,250 tonnes of durum wheat donated by Libya to Iraq is unloading at Jordan's Red Sea port of Aqaba, Jordanian shipping sources said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The Panama-flagged vessel Madeira, which left the Libyan port of Benghazi en route to Iraq last week, arrived on Wednesday.</p>
<p>They said Libya had bought the wheat from Swiss supplier Andre.</p>
<p>-- Amman Newsroom +9626-623776</p>
</text>
